# VRAG-012: the held-out Q&A set is sealed by the sha256 of its bytes — the digest is
# recorded in README.md and re-checked by `make heldout-check`. This repo is worked on from
# Windows, where `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout; that changes the bytes
# and the seal fails on a fresh clone for a reason that has nothing to do with the labels.
# Pin the eval files to LF everywhere so the digest is the same on every machine.
*.jsonl text eol=lf

# Same reason, one step removed: `make corpus-check` asserts the manifest reproduces
# byte-for-byte against the pinned dataset revision (VRAG-004).
data/corpus/manifest.json text eol=lf

# Same reason again, and this one bites inside a container rather than in a digest:
# docker/ollama-init.sh is bind-mounted into the ollama image and run by `sh`. Checked out
# with CRLF it fails on `set -eu\r` with an error that names neither the file nor the cause.
*.sh text eol=lf
